evaluation, development, and commercial production purposes, including as a
backend component of your own applications and services offered to customers.
Charging for those applications and services is permitted, subject to
section 4's restriction on offering Obol itself as a service.

You may keep private image mirrors, offline bundles, backups, and disaster
recovery copies for those purposes. Employees, contractors, hosting providers,
and auditors may receive or access copies solely to operate, support, secure,
or audit your permitted installations on your behalf. You remain responsible
for their compliance with these terms.

This permission does not expire for a version validly obtained under this
